    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d524">

                <pb facs="0830" n="820" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg820"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Lieutenant General Albert C.
                            Wedemeyer to the Chief of Staff</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Eisenhower</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-02-18">18 February
                        1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>201. General Marshall’s present view re head for MAG,<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d524-f1"/> my 20766,<anchor n="20" xml:id="d524-f2"/> para 4 refers,
                    follows. Initially will be assigned to Executive Headquarters in Peiping. The
                    Executive Headquarters will continue at least to the end of the year, however,
                    by that time the American representatives of that headquarters may appropriately
                    function under the Military Advisory Group at which time General Marshall
                    suggests placing Gillem<anchor n="21" xml:id="d524-f3"/> in charge of MAG.</p>
                <p>Major General Robert B. McClure will continue to serve as acting head MAG and
                    could be retained as deputy head subject to decision of the officer designated
                    to head MAG.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
